1
00:00:01,436 --> 00:00:04,526
[monitor beeping]

2
00:00:08,138 --> 00:00:11,011
[monitor tone]

3
00:00:14,144 --> 00:00:16,451
[roosters cawing]

4
00:00:18,540 --> 00:00:21,456
[mystical music]

5
00:00:24,763 --> 00:00:27,157
- [Hiraku] I was dreaming?

6
00:00:28,854 --> 00:00:31,248
It's been a long time
since I've dreamt that.

7
00:00:39,735 --> 00:00:40,953
- Lord Hiraku.

8
00:00:41,084 --> 00:00:42,433
I'm terribly sorry,

9
00:00:42,564 --> 00:00:45,088
I still haven't finished
the morning chores.

10
00:00:45,219 --> 00:00:49,397
- Don't worry,
I woke up early today.

11
00:00:49,527 --> 00:00:54,184
Anyways, I'd appreciate it if
you stopped calling me lord.

12
00:00:54,315 --> 00:00:57,231
- Right, very well, mayor.

13
00:00:57,361 --> 00:00:59,189
- [Maid] Oh, good morning.

14
00:00:59,320 --> 00:01:02,932
- [Hiraku] Ha, good morning.
[sighs]

15
00:01:03,063 --> 00:01:04,499
[stuff crashes]

16
00:01:04,629 --> 00:01:06,457
[slime bubbling]

17
00:01:06,588 --> 00:01:09,025
- Sorry, I was being careless.

18
00:01:09,156 --> 00:01:11,245
- So you're working in
the kitchen now?

19
00:01:11,375 --> 00:01:13,595
- I'll just roast
the whole thing.

20
00:01:13,725 --> 00:01:15,423
- [Hiraku] No, cut him
some slack.

21
00:01:15,553 --> 00:01:17,468
[slime vocalizes]

22
00:01:17,599 --> 00:01:20,428
[cheerful pastoral music]

23
00:01:21,516 --> 00:01:22,430
[Hiraku exhales]

24
00:01:22,560 --> 00:01:24,562
- Oh?

25
00:01:24,693 --> 00:01:26,086
What a surprise.

26
00:01:26,216 --> 00:01:27,826
You're up early today,
aren't you?

27
00:01:27,957 --> 00:01:30,742
- I am, I wanted to get
an early start.

28
00:01:30,873 --> 00:01:32,309
- [Tia] Good morning.

29
00:01:34,703 --> 00:01:36,270
- What are you doing here?

30
00:01:36,400 --> 00:01:38,446
- I had to talk to Granmary
about something

31
00:01:38,576 --> 00:01:40,100
while she was on patrol duty.

32
00:01:40,230 --> 00:01:41,318
- [Lu] Is there a problem?

33
00:01:41,449 --> 00:01:43,233
- It's nothing like that.

34
00:01:43,364 --> 00:01:45,931
She reported to me earlier
about something, and...

35
00:01:46,062 --> 00:01:47,542
[Lu and Tia hum]

36
00:01:47,672 --> 00:01:49,761
Is something wrong?

37
00:01:49,892 --> 00:01:50,806
- Hm?

38
00:01:50,936 --> 00:01:52,590
No, it's nothing.

39
00:01:52,721 --> 00:01:54,549
I just had a dream
I haven't had in a while.

40
00:01:54,679 --> 00:01:55,985
- [Lu] A dream?

41
00:01:56,116 --> 00:01:59,728
- Well, actually, it's
more like an old memory.

42
00:01:59,858 --> 00:02:02,383
[children giggling]

43
00:02:02,513 --> 00:02:05,995
[upbeat pastoral music]

44
00:02:29,671 --> 00:02:34,154
Back then, I really never
could have imagined,

45
00:02:40,595 --> 00:02:44,294
that I'd ever get to live
such a dream of a life.

46
00:02:45,774 --> 00:02:48,951
["Flower Ring" by
Shino Shimoji, Aya Suzaki plays]

47
00:04:16,995 --> 00:04:18,954
- [God] Hiraku Machio.

48
00:04:19,084 --> 00:04:21,435
That's you, isn't it?

49
00:04:21,565 --> 00:04:22,566
- [Hiraku] Yes?

50
00:04:22,697 --> 00:04:24,176
And, um, you are?

51
00:04:24,307 --> 00:04:26,831
- [God] I'm the god who
watches over this world.

52
00:04:26,962 --> 00:04:28,442
- [Hiraku] You're God?

53
00:04:28,572 --> 00:04:31,575
Ah, I guess that means
I finally died.

54
00:04:31,706 --> 00:04:33,273
- [God] Indeed.

55
00:04:33,403 --> 00:04:36,101
According to this world's
calendar you've lived 39 years.

56
00:04:36,232 --> 00:04:38,147
And what a cruel life it was.

57
00:04:38,278 --> 00:04:39,670
You were betrayed by others,

58
00:04:39,801 --> 00:04:42,282
and then fell ill with
a terminal disease.

59
00:04:42,412 --> 00:04:44,675
That's why, I've decided
to give you a chance

60
00:04:44,806 --> 00:04:46,111
at a second life.

61
00:04:46,242 --> 00:04:47,287
- [Hiraku] You can do that?

62
00:04:47,417 --> 00:04:49,289
- [God] Of course, I'm God.

63
00:04:49,419 --> 00:04:51,508
This time I shall grant you
a healthy body

64
00:04:51,639 --> 00:04:53,031
that won't fall ill.

65
00:04:53,162 --> 00:04:56,121
You see, I consider it
a mistake on my part

66
00:04:56,252 --> 00:04:57,601
that you were forced to live

67
00:04:57,732 --> 00:04:59,690
such a cruel existence
in the first place.

68
00:04:59,821 --> 00:05:01,039
- [Hiraku] Your mistake?

69
00:05:01,170 --> 00:05:02,650
- [God] I ask that you
take this act

70
00:05:02,780 --> 00:05:04,565
as penance for my misdeed.

71
00:05:04,695 --> 00:05:07,829
- [Hiraku] Oh, I don't really
get it, but okay.

72
00:05:07,959 --> 00:05:09,961
- [God] Well, let's make sure
to do this right.

73
00:05:10,092 --> 00:05:12,094
Do you have any requests?

74
00:05:12,224 --> 00:05:14,531
I'll let you live your new life
the way you want to.

75
00:05:14,662 --> 00:05:16,185
- [Hiraku] The way I want to?

76
00:05:16,316 --> 00:05:18,579
- [God] I can grant pretty much
any request you have.

77
00:05:18,709 --> 00:05:20,581
- [Hiraku] In that case,
I've got it,

78
00:05:20,711 --> 00:05:22,278
I want to try my hand
at farming.

79
00:05:22,409 --> 00:05:24,019
- [God] Farming?

80
00:05:24,149 --> 00:05:26,021
- [Hiraku] Yeah, I really
liked watching a show

81
00:05:26,151 --> 00:05:27,936
about farming while I was
stuck in the hospital.

82
00:05:28,066 --> 00:05:29,067
- [God] Mm-hmm.

83
00:05:29,198 --> 00:05:30,155
- [Hiraku] It was a show

84
00:05:30,286 --> 00:05:31,461
about celebrities farming.

85
00:05:31,592 --> 00:05:32,984
In my last life,
I had a hard time

86
00:05:33,115 --> 00:05:34,899
getting along with
other people,

87
00:05:35,030 --> 00:05:36,510
so I thought it would be nice

88
00:05:36,640 --> 00:05:38,207
if I could live a laid back
life of farming

89
00:05:38,338 --> 00:05:40,383
somewhere where
not many people go.

90
00:05:40,514 --> 00:05:41,558
Is that too much to ask?

91
00:05:41,689 --> 00:05:42,951
- [God] No, it's just that

92
00:05:43,081 --> 00:05:44,648
farming isn't part of
my jurisdiction.

93
00:05:44,779 --> 00:05:46,128
- [Hiraku] Your jurisdiction?

94
00:05:46,258 --> 00:05:48,522
- [God] But let's give 'em
a call and see.

95
00:05:48,652 --> 00:05:51,742
Ah, hm, okay.

96
00:05:51,873 --> 00:05:54,310
It is done, you'll
receive your new life

97
00:05:54,441 --> 00:05:56,530
and a healthy body
with which to live it.

98
00:05:56,660 --> 00:05:59,228
I've also received permission
from the god of agriculture

99
00:05:59,359 --> 00:06:03,145
to bestow upon you the power of
the almighty farming tool.

100
00:06:03,275 --> 00:06:05,408
- [Hiraku] The almighty
farming tool?

101
00:06:05,539 --> 00:06:09,847
- [God] Now then, enjoy your
chance at a second life.

102
00:06:09,978 --> 00:06:12,676
[mystical music]

103
00:06:15,375 --> 00:06:17,768
[Hiraku grunting]

104
00:06:17,899 --> 00:06:21,424
[leaves rustling]

105
00:06:28,344 --> 00:06:30,128
- My body can move.

106
00:06:31,869 --> 00:06:34,829
It's been a long time since
I've been able to move around.

107
00:06:34,959 --> 00:06:37,962
How many years has it been
since I could stand?

108
00:06:39,964 --> 00:06:42,358
Having a healthy body,
is amazing.

109
00:06:43,925 --> 00:06:47,015
Alright, I've come back
to life safe and sound.

110
00:06:47,145 --> 00:06:49,234
It's time to start
my second life,

111
00:06:49,365 --> 00:06:51,976
the farming life
that I wished for.

112
00:06:52,107 --> 00:06:53,848
[Hiraku giggling]

113
00:06:53,978 --> 00:06:56,372
[playful music]

114
00:07:00,681 --> 00:07:03,118
So this is where I start?

115
00:07:06,730 --> 00:07:10,908
Forest, forest as far as
the eye can see, hmm.

116
00:07:11,039 --> 00:07:13,911
I know I asked for somewhere
that not many people go,

117
00:07:14,042 --> 00:07:15,478
but this almost feels
like a place

118
00:07:15,609 --> 00:07:17,524
that people can't reach
even if they want to.

119
00:07:17,654 --> 00:07:20,048
Oh well, no use
in complaining now.

120
00:07:20,178 --> 00:07:22,442
I need to think about
what I can do from here.

121
00:07:22,572 --> 00:07:25,270
I'm dressed like a villager
from a video game.

122
00:07:25,401 --> 00:07:28,360
And I get the feeling that
I'm younger than I used to be.

123
00:07:28,491 --> 00:07:30,885
Do I have anything
I can actually use?

124
00:07:31,015 --> 00:07:34,149
That's right,
the almighty farming tool.

125
00:07:34,279 --> 00:07:37,195
[mystical music]

126
00:07:39,110 --> 00:07:40,764
[Hiraku chuckles]

127
00:07:40,895 --> 00:07:43,201
This is it, here we go.

128
00:07:43,332 --> 00:07:44,942
[Hiraku grunts]

129
00:07:45,073 --> 00:07:46,161
[Hiraku chuckles]

130
00:07:46,291 --> 00:07:48,032
This must be magic.

131
00:07:48,163 --> 00:07:50,992
No matter how much I use
this tool, I don't get tired.

132
00:07:51,122 --> 00:07:52,254
I can till the hard ground

133
00:07:52,384 --> 00:07:54,474
and cut through tree roots
no problem.

134
00:07:55,431 --> 00:07:57,477
The soil is nice and fluffy.

135
00:07:57,607 --> 00:07:59,435
I'm sure I can grow
some great vegetables

136
00:07:59,566 --> 00:08:01,611
in a field I till with this.
Wait a minute.

137
00:08:01,742 --> 00:08:04,571
I need to worry about finding
water and food right now.

138
00:08:04,701 --> 00:08:07,487
[quirky music]

139
00:08:07,617 --> 00:08:10,141
The forest goes on and on.

140
00:08:10,272 --> 00:08:11,708
I tried listening carefully

141
00:08:11,839 --> 00:08:13,797
so that I could hear if
any streams were nearby,

142
00:08:13,928 --> 00:08:16,670
but all I could hear was
the rustling of the leaves.

143
00:08:16,800 --> 00:08:19,063
Forget finding edible plants,

144
00:08:19,194 --> 00:08:21,413
I don't see any grass
growing around here.

145
00:08:21,544 --> 00:08:23,677
Am I playing on the right
difficulty setting?

146
00:08:23,807 --> 00:08:26,244
[gentle suspenseful music]

147
00:08:26,375 --> 00:08:30,335
Now that I think about it,
there's a good chance

148
00:08:30,466 --> 00:08:32,816
that there could be dangerous
animals around here.

149
00:08:32,947 --> 00:08:35,297
I need to hurry and
find somewhere safe.

150
00:08:41,129 --> 00:08:46,003
Whoa, that's one nice tree.

151
00:08:46,134 --> 00:08:47,918
It'll make a good landmark,

152
00:08:48,049 --> 00:08:50,268
I think I'll set up
my base camp here.

153
00:08:50,399 --> 00:08:53,271
[quirky music]

154
00:08:53,402 --> 00:08:55,752
I walked around for a while,

155
00:08:55,883 --> 00:08:58,581
but there don't seem to be
any rivers or ponds nearby.

156
00:08:58,712 --> 00:09:01,584
In that case, I'll dig a well.

157
00:09:03,064 --> 00:09:04,631
I bet you're thinking
that it's silly

158
00:09:04,761 --> 00:09:06,633
to try to find water
underground like this.

159
00:09:06,763 --> 00:09:09,287
But I've heard that people
sometimes use this method

160
00:09:09,418 --> 00:09:12,334
to find water pipes, maybe.

161
00:09:12,464 --> 00:09:14,075
I don't get this at all.

162
00:09:14,205 --> 00:09:16,904
Shovel!

163
00:09:17,034 --> 00:09:19,123
This almighty farming tool
really lives up to its name.

164
00:09:19,254 --> 00:09:21,125
It can turn into
all kinds of stuff.

165
00:09:21,256 --> 00:09:24,259
- Excavator!
- It can't turn into
complicated machines, though.

166
00:09:24,389 --> 00:09:26,522
[Hiraku grunting]

167
00:09:26,653 --> 00:09:28,437
Just as I expected,

168
00:09:28,568 --> 00:09:30,352
I don't get tired
no matter how much I dig.

169
00:09:30,482 --> 00:09:33,050
Now I can dig forever
until I hit water.

170
00:09:33,181 --> 00:09:35,270
[Hiraku panting]

171
00:09:35,400 --> 00:09:37,272
Am I stuck down here?

172
00:09:37,402 --> 00:09:39,404
I know, I'll dig diagonally.

173
00:09:39,535 --> 00:09:41,058
[playful music]

174
00:09:42,364 --> 00:09:45,497
[water trickling]

175
00:09:46,629 --> 00:09:48,544
I only just started digging.

176
00:09:48,675 --> 00:09:50,502
It's my lucky day.

177
00:09:50,633 --> 00:09:54,115
No, this might be another
one of God's blessings.

178
00:09:54,245 --> 00:09:57,640
Now that I've secured water,
it's time to find food.

179
00:09:57,771 --> 00:09:59,381
That was my plan,

180
00:09:59,511 --> 00:10:03,037
but oddly enough,
I don't feel hungry at all.

181
00:10:03,167 --> 00:10:06,170
I wonder if this is the power of
the almighty farming tool.

182
00:10:06,301 --> 00:10:07,519
It's probably dangerous

183
00:10:07,650 --> 00:10:09,870
to go wandering through
the forest again.

184
00:10:10,000 --> 00:10:12,655
Scythe.

185
00:10:12,786 --> 00:10:15,005
Since I'm going to turn this
into my base of operations,

186
00:10:15,136 --> 00:10:16,964
I'll keep working on
building it up.

187
00:10:17,094 --> 00:10:18,574
It'd be nice if I found
something to eat

188
00:10:18,705 --> 00:10:20,010
while I was working here.

189
00:10:20,141 --> 00:10:23,666
But I don't see anything
around here. Oh well.

190
00:10:26,756 --> 00:10:28,932
If I'm going to cultivate
the land here,

191
00:10:29,063 --> 00:10:31,282
this tree is going to be
in the way eventually.

192
00:10:31,413 --> 00:10:32,719
Hmm.

193
00:10:32,849 --> 00:10:34,677
It looks like
a pretty sturdy tree,

194
00:10:34,808 --> 00:10:37,288
but maybe if I turn the
almighty tool into an ax

195
00:10:37,419 --> 00:10:38,899
I can cut it down.

196
00:10:39,029 --> 00:10:41,162
I think the right way is
to start cutting one side,

197
00:10:41,292 --> 00:10:43,730
and then go in from
the other side with the ax.

198
00:10:43,860 --> 00:10:45,035
I did it.

199
00:10:45,993 --> 00:10:47,603
Hm, okay then.

200
00:10:47,734 --> 00:10:49,300
I'll start from this side.

201
00:10:49,431 --> 00:10:50,911
Here we go!

202
00:10:52,347 --> 00:10:54,088
[dramatic pastoral music]

203
00:10:54,218 --> 00:10:56,177
What the?

204
00:10:56,307 --> 00:10:58,962
[screams]

205
00:11:04,968 --> 00:11:06,970
I cut it clean with one swing.

206
00:11:07,101 --> 00:11:10,017
This almighty farming tool
is something else.

207
00:11:10,147 --> 00:11:11,235
[Hiraku laughing]

208
00:11:11,366 --> 00:11:12,367
Hatchet.

209
00:11:12,497 --> 00:11:13,455
Since I've already cut it down,

210
00:11:13,585 --> 00:11:15,022
I should process it into lumber.

211
00:11:15,152 --> 00:11:17,154
I'll start by cutting off
the branches,

212
00:11:17,285 --> 00:11:19,809
then cut up the trunk
and strip the bark off.

213
00:11:19,940 --> 00:11:21,332
I'm cutting through
this sturdy tree

214
00:11:21,463 --> 00:11:23,073
like it's a block of cheese.

215
00:11:23,204 --> 00:11:24,553
So about this hook-like tool

216
00:11:24,684 --> 00:11:26,337
that I'm using to
drag the tree around.

217
00:11:26,468 --> 00:11:27,774
I'm not sure what it's called,

218
00:11:27,904 --> 00:11:29,689
but apparently I can turn
the almighty tool

219
00:11:29,819 --> 00:11:31,168
into anything I can imagine.

220
00:11:31,299 --> 00:11:32,561
[cheerful music]

221
00:11:32,692 --> 00:11:34,824
Now I've got myself some lumber.

222
00:11:34,955 --> 00:11:37,653
Based on the farming sim games
I used to play,

223
00:11:37,784 --> 00:11:40,525
this is about the time I should
start building a small hut.

224
00:11:40,656 --> 00:11:42,092
But it's not going to be easy

225
00:11:42,223 --> 00:11:44,355
to build the parts for
the walls and roof.

226
00:11:44,486 --> 00:11:47,576
Plus, I don't have any nails or
glue to stick them together.

227
00:11:47,707 --> 00:11:49,665
Building a hut from scratch
is tougher than I thought.

228
00:11:49,796 --> 00:11:53,495
Hm, this pillar I stuck in
the ground for fun

229
00:11:53,625 --> 00:11:56,541
is casting a shadow
almost like a sun dial.

230
00:11:56,672 --> 00:11:59,457
Oh no, I was having so much fun
that I lost track of time.

231
00:11:59,588 --> 00:12:02,069
The sun's about to set and
then it's going to be night.

232
00:12:02,199 --> 00:12:03,157
What happens then?

233
00:12:03,287 --> 00:12:04,288
It's going to be dark out.

234
00:12:04,419 --> 00:12:05,550
I need some kind of light.

235
00:12:05,681 --> 00:12:07,074
Flashlight, lamp.

236
00:12:07,204 --> 00:12:09,598
No good, I'll need to
start a fire.

237
00:12:09,729 --> 00:12:11,382
Lighter, some matches?

238
00:12:11,513 --> 00:12:14,429
Crap, maybe this has to do with
that jurisdiction thing.

239
00:12:14,559 --> 00:12:17,824
Turning the almighty tool
into a match is just stupid.

240
00:12:17,954 --> 00:12:20,609
I need something that can
create heat without burning up.

241
00:12:20,740 --> 00:12:23,220
Bingo! Magnifying glass.

242
00:12:23,351 --> 00:12:24,656
[mystical music]

243
00:12:24,787 --> 00:12:27,137
It worked, I can start
a fire with this.

244
00:12:27,268 --> 00:12:29,444
If it was daytime.

245
00:12:29,574 --> 00:12:32,360
[quirky music]

246
00:12:34,710 --> 00:12:37,757
I ended up quickly carving a
hole into the tree's trunk

247
00:12:37,887 --> 00:12:39,497
so I'd have
some kind of shelter.

248
00:12:39,628 --> 00:12:41,761
I thought about digging
a hole in the ground,

249
00:12:41,891 --> 00:12:44,764
but the thought of accidentally
burying myself alive scared me.

250
00:12:44,894 --> 00:12:49,681
This chisel is another form
of the almighty farming tool.

251
00:12:49,812 --> 00:12:52,206
It looks like it'll take
a lot of trial and error

252
00:12:52,336 --> 00:12:55,992
before I can make
furniture or a hut.

253
00:12:56,123 --> 00:12:58,734
I was worried I wouldn't be able
to see when it was dark,

254
00:12:58,865 --> 00:13:01,128
but I'm surprised at
how well I can.

255
00:13:01,258 --> 00:13:03,608
Maybe it's because when God
granted me a healthy body,

256
00:13:03,739 --> 00:13:05,523
my vision improved as well.

257
00:13:05,654 --> 00:13:06,742
[gentle music]

258
00:13:06,873 --> 00:13:08,526
Or maybe, it's because of those,

259
00:13:08,657 --> 00:13:12,139
the two moons casting light.

260
00:13:12,269 --> 00:13:16,273
Wow, I really am in
another world, aren't I?

261
00:13:21,713 --> 00:13:23,803
[leaves rustling]

262
00:13:23,933 --> 00:13:25,630
I messed around a lot
trying to figure out

263
00:13:25,761 --> 00:13:27,110
how to work with the lumber,

264
00:13:27,241 --> 00:13:29,809
and before I knew it,
morning had come.

265
00:13:29,939 --> 00:13:31,332
[gentle music]

266
00:13:31,462 --> 00:13:33,160
[water trickling]

267
00:13:36,816 --> 00:13:39,731
It looks like I'll be fine
in terms of having water.

268
00:13:39,862 --> 00:13:41,908
Right, I almost forgot.

269
00:13:42,038 --> 00:13:43,648
[fire crackling]

270
00:13:43,779 --> 00:13:46,956
[Hiraku blowing]

271
00:13:48,131 --> 00:13:50,220
And now I have a fire going.

272
00:13:50,351 --> 00:13:52,179
Heave-ho, heave-ho,
heave-ho, heave-ho.

273
00:13:52,309 --> 00:13:53,876
From there, I continued
clearing the area

274
00:13:54,007 --> 00:13:55,747
so that I could
cultivate the land.

275
00:13:55,878 --> 00:13:57,227
I don't get tired or hungry

276
00:13:57,358 --> 00:13:59,142
while using the
almighty farming tool,

277
00:13:59,273 --> 00:14:00,883
but I'm sure that
doing this kind of work

278
00:14:01,014 --> 00:14:03,233
is using up some of
my body's stamina.

279
00:14:03,364 --> 00:14:06,584
Even specks of dust can
pile up to make mountains.

280
00:14:06,715 --> 00:14:09,674
I think it's finally time
for me to eat something.

281
00:14:09,805 --> 00:14:11,415
It might be time to change gears

282
00:14:11,546 --> 00:14:13,591
and go look for food
somewhere further away.

283
00:14:13,722 --> 00:14:15,724
[galloping]

284
00:14:15,855 --> 00:14:16,725
[dramatic music]

285
00:14:16,856 --> 00:14:18,422
[snarling]

286
00:14:19,728 --> 00:14:21,556
What is that thing?

287
00:14:27,170 --> 00:14:28,302
[jaunty music]

288
00:14:28,432 --> 00:14:30,391
Well that was a happy accident.

289
00:14:30,521 --> 00:14:32,523
I had no choice but to kill it.

290
00:14:32,654 --> 00:14:34,786
It had scary fangs and stuff.

291
00:14:34,917 --> 00:14:36,701
All it took was
one blow to the neck

292
00:14:36,832 --> 00:14:38,878
with the almighty farming tool.

293
00:14:39,008 --> 00:14:40,488
I tilled the giant rabbit's head

294
00:14:40,618 --> 00:14:43,012
and turned it into
a nice fluffy soil.

295
00:14:43,143 --> 00:14:45,058
Then I turned the
almighty tool into a knife

296
00:14:45,188 --> 00:14:47,364
and used it to
take apart the body.

297
00:14:47,495 --> 00:14:49,584
At least I'll be able
to feed myself.

298
00:14:49,714 --> 00:14:51,412
I'm thankful for that.

299
00:14:51,542 --> 00:14:54,937
Grilled rabbit,
it tastes very natural.

300
00:14:55,068 --> 00:14:58,071
Or rather, it tastes
gamey and bloody.

301
00:14:58,201 --> 00:15:01,161
Still, I'm grateful that
I have something to eat.

302
00:15:02,336 --> 00:15:05,078
But, what goes in
must also come out.

303
00:15:05,208 --> 00:15:07,167
The next thing I built
was a toilet.

304
00:15:07,297 --> 00:15:08,429
[jaunty music]

305
00:15:08,559 --> 00:15:10,692
The toilet seat was
made from a log.

306
00:15:10,822 --> 00:15:12,912
Below that, I dug a hole.

307
00:15:13,042 --> 00:15:14,826
[Hiraku sighs]

308
00:15:14,957 --> 00:15:18,178
Now I can relax and
take care of my business.

309
00:15:18,308 --> 00:15:20,441
[leaves rustling]

310
00:15:24,184 --> 00:15:26,012
I can't relax at all.

311
00:15:26,142 --> 00:15:29,189
I couldn't sleep either so I
used my building knowledge.

312
00:15:29,319 --> 00:15:30,407
It ended up being better built

313
00:15:30,538 --> 00:15:32,453
than where I actually
slept, but.

314
00:15:32,583 --> 00:15:33,715
[Hiraku sighs]

315
00:15:33,845 --> 00:15:35,108
A toilet that's
comfortable to use

316
00:15:35,238 --> 00:15:37,023
is necessary for
any sort of civilized life.

317
00:15:37,153 --> 00:15:39,503
[bright music]

318
00:15:41,766 --> 00:15:43,943
I took a bunch of detours
getting here,

319
00:15:44,073 --> 00:15:46,336
but I've finally started
cultivating the land.

320
00:15:46,467 --> 00:15:50,079
What should I grow to help
support my life here?

321
00:15:50,210 --> 00:15:52,125
I'll need stuff that
preserves well.

322
00:15:52,255 --> 00:15:53,561
Potatoes?

323
00:15:53,691 --> 00:15:54,954
Onions?

324
00:15:55,084 --> 00:15:56,694
Some tomatoes and cucumbers
would be nice.

325
00:15:56,825 --> 00:15:58,174
You can eat those as is.

326
00:15:58,305 --> 00:16:02,483
Cabbage and spinach,
daikon, napa, carrots.

327
00:16:02,613 --> 00:16:05,181
Oh, I want to eat
some boiled corn, too.

328
00:16:07,749 --> 00:16:10,447
I've realized something here.

329
00:16:10,578 --> 00:16:12,058
Even if I cultivate the land,

330
00:16:12,188 --> 00:16:14,930
I have no seeds
or seedlings to plant.

331
00:16:15,061 --> 00:16:16,323
I guess my only option

332
00:16:16,453 --> 00:16:18,238
is to look for
something in the forest.

333
00:16:18,368 --> 00:16:21,284
I went to bed on a stomach
full of rabbit meat

334
00:16:21,415 --> 00:16:23,025
when I woke up the next morning,

335
00:16:23,156 --> 00:16:25,897
my eyes opened in surprise
when they saw this.

336
00:16:26,028 --> 00:16:27,508
[Hiraku chuckling]

337
00:16:27,638 --> 00:16:29,031
Can the plants
in this world grow

338
00:16:29,162 --> 00:16:31,120
even if you don't
plant their seeds?

339
00:16:31,251 --> 00:16:33,557
Or could this be because of
the almighty tool?

340
00:16:33,688 --> 00:16:35,820
There are sprouts
popping up in every row,

341
00:16:35,951 --> 00:16:37,648
and it only took one night.

342
00:16:37,779 --> 00:16:38,910
But these sprouts look different

343
00:16:39,041 --> 00:16:40,738
than the plants
I'm used to seeing.

344
00:16:40,869 --> 00:16:43,741
Those kind of look like
scallions, but they're bent.

345
00:16:43,872 --> 00:16:45,830
Well, I'm not sure
what they are,

346
00:16:45,961 --> 00:16:48,703
but even so I know
what I have to do.

347
00:16:48,833 --> 00:16:50,879
I need to protect these fields
from those giant rabbits

348
00:16:51,010 --> 00:16:53,186
and any other beasts
that live in this forest.

349
00:16:53,316 --> 00:16:55,144
[Hiraku grunting]

350
00:16:55,275 --> 00:16:58,060
First, I'll build a fence
around the perimeter.

351
00:16:58,191 --> 00:16:59,844
Then, I'll dig a ditch
around the fence.

352
00:16:59,975 --> 00:17:01,281
[bright music]

353
00:17:01,411 --> 00:17:02,717
I'm still a little worried,

354
00:17:02,847 --> 00:17:04,762
but I feel a lot better
having this built.

355
00:17:04,893 --> 00:17:09,245
After a few days, the fence
and the ditch were completed.

356
00:17:09,376 --> 00:17:11,639
During that time, I fed myself
from another rabbit

357
00:17:11,769 --> 00:17:13,771
that tried charging
into my fields.

358
00:17:13,902 --> 00:17:16,252
I wonder why they always
charge in headfirst like that.

359
00:17:16,383 --> 00:17:18,559
Maybe I'm what they're
trying to attack and eat.

360
00:17:18,689 --> 00:17:20,735
[bright music]

361
00:17:21,910 --> 00:17:24,043
Nature.

362
00:17:24,173 --> 00:17:25,783
If I water them with
the watering pot

363
00:17:25,914 --> 00:17:29,048
from the almighty farming tool,
they get bigger every day.

364
00:17:29,178 --> 00:17:32,486
They're definitely growing
a lot faster than normal plants.

365
00:17:32,616 --> 00:17:35,576
I'm still not exactly sure
what I'm growing,

366
00:17:35,706 --> 00:17:37,752
but I hope it's stuff
that I can eat.

367
00:17:37,882 --> 00:17:40,015
If they all turned out
to be decorative plants.

368
00:17:40,146 --> 00:17:43,236
[Hiraku screams]

369
00:17:43,366 --> 00:17:46,326
I'm sure that I'd fall
to my knees in despair.

370
00:17:46,456 --> 00:17:47,283
[Hiraku sighs]

371
00:17:47,414 --> 00:17:48,937
A few more days passed.

372
00:17:49,068 --> 00:17:51,809
After all my hard work,
I was able to build a small hut.

373
00:17:51,940 --> 00:17:53,202
I cut grooves into the wood

374
00:17:53,333 --> 00:17:55,030
and stacked them
on top of each other.

375
00:17:55,161 --> 00:17:56,945
It's basically a log house.

376
00:17:57,076 --> 00:17:59,034
Part of the way through
I wasn't able to lift the lumber

377
00:17:59,165 --> 00:18:01,906
up to the top anymore,
so I dug out the ground a bit

378
00:18:02,037 --> 00:18:03,647
to give myself more room.

379
00:18:03,778 --> 00:18:05,606
For the roof, I used
bark from the trees

380
00:18:05,736 --> 00:18:09,218
and held it down with nails
I made from shaved down wood.

381
00:18:09,349 --> 00:18:10,480
If I was in a fairy-tale,

382
00:18:10,611 --> 00:18:11,916
a wolf would be able
to huff and puff

383
00:18:12,047 --> 00:18:13,657
and blow this house down,

384
00:18:13,788 --> 00:18:15,398
but I thought it was
a lot more civilized

385
00:18:15,529 --> 00:18:17,096
than living in a tree hole.

386
00:18:17,226 --> 00:18:20,664
I can't wait to see
how my crops turn out.

387
00:18:21,665 --> 00:18:23,493
I feel really motivated lately,

388
00:18:23,624 --> 00:18:26,017
and I've been looking
forward to each new day.

389
00:18:26,148 --> 00:18:27,976
That was when I started
to get into a routine

390
00:18:28,107 --> 00:18:30,065
with my new life here.

391
00:18:33,155 --> 00:18:35,026
Dogs?

392
00:18:35,157 --> 00:18:36,724
They're huge.

393
00:18:36,854 --> 00:18:40,162
They don't seem like
they're going to attack me.

394
00:18:40,293 --> 00:18:42,512
And they look like they're
in pretty rough shape.

395
00:18:42,643 --> 00:18:44,035
[dog whimpers]

396
00:18:46,908 --> 00:18:49,302
- [chuckles] Come on.

397
00:18:51,869 --> 00:18:54,045
Perfect timing,
I just killed a boar

398
00:18:54,176 --> 00:18:56,265
and didn't know what to do
with all the meat.

399
00:18:56,396 --> 00:18:57,875
It was trying to get
over my fence

400
00:18:58,006 --> 00:19:00,443
so I had no choice
but to exterminate it.

401
00:19:00,574 --> 00:19:02,532
One of them has a swollen belly.

402
00:19:02,663 --> 00:19:04,708
I wonder if he was trying to
take the pregnant one

403
00:19:04,839 --> 00:19:08,364
somewhere safe when they were
attacked by some other animal.

404
00:19:08,495 --> 00:19:10,105
This reminds me of when
I was a kid

405
00:19:10,236 --> 00:19:13,369
and I wanted to get a dog.

406
00:19:13,500 --> 00:19:15,458
They say that dogs are
a farmer's friend.

407
00:19:15,589 --> 00:19:18,200
It'd be nice if they
hung around here.

408
00:19:18,331 --> 00:19:19,941
[Dog whining]

409
00:19:20,071 --> 00:19:20,985
What's wrong?

410
00:19:21,116 --> 00:19:23,640
[dog growls]

411
00:19:23,771 --> 00:19:28,210
Is she about to
give birth, here, now?

412
00:19:28,341 --> 00:19:30,995
What should I do?
How can I help?

413
00:19:31,126 --> 00:19:34,216
Well, it's probably better
than being outside

414
00:19:34,347 --> 00:19:36,000
so I led them into my house.

415
00:19:36,131 --> 00:19:39,308
How long does it take
for dogs to give birth?

416
00:19:39,439 --> 00:19:40,788
Does she need water to drink?

417
00:19:40,918 --> 00:19:42,833
It'll get colder
once the sun sets.

418
00:19:42,964 --> 00:19:44,313
I should build a fire here.

419
00:19:44,444 --> 00:19:46,054
But that'll fill
the room with smoke.

420
00:19:46,185 --> 00:19:48,361
Maybe I can leave it
just outside the door.

421
00:19:48,491 --> 00:19:50,754
[dog whimpering]

422
00:19:54,280 --> 00:19:57,283
I tried doing everything
I could think of to help.

423
00:19:57,413 --> 00:19:59,850
And I figured it wasn't good
for a human to be around,

424
00:19:59,981 --> 00:20:01,678
so I left them alone.

425
00:20:03,898 --> 00:20:08,337
I hope I didn't end up bothering
them by trying to help too much.

426
00:20:08,468 --> 00:20:10,818
If that giant boar attacked
while she was giving birth

427
00:20:10,948 --> 00:20:12,994
and unable to move,

428
00:20:13,124 --> 00:20:15,214
[gentle suspenseful music]

429
00:20:16,215 --> 00:20:17,477
It might be because of the light

430
00:20:17,607 --> 00:20:19,392
from the fire next to the hut,

431
00:20:19,522 --> 00:20:21,698
but everything else looks
really dark tonight.

432
00:20:27,661 --> 00:20:28,792
[Hiraku sighs]

433
00:20:28,923 --> 00:20:29,750
[Hiraku grunts]

434
00:20:29,880 --> 00:20:32,056
Oh no, I fell asleep.

435
00:20:38,062 --> 00:20:40,369
Uh, I'm coming in.

436
00:20:41,327 --> 00:20:43,894
[puppies yapping]

437
00:20:44,025 --> 00:20:46,854
[gentle cheerful music]

438
00:20:46,984 --> 00:20:49,291
They look calm
now that it's all over,

439
00:20:49,422 --> 00:20:51,554
but I'm sure she had
a really tough night.

440
00:20:51,685 --> 00:20:53,904
Oh yeah.

441
00:20:54,035 --> 00:20:55,645
To celebrate her giving birth,

442
00:20:55,776 --> 00:21:00,259
I cut up the tastiest
looking parts from the boar.

443
00:21:00,389 --> 00:21:03,131
I thought the dogs would go off
somewhere after she gave birth,

444
00:21:03,262 --> 00:21:06,830
but it looks like they're
going to hang around here.

445
00:21:06,961 --> 00:21:09,616
Since it seems like they're
really attached to that hut,

446
00:21:09,746 --> 00:21:11,835
I can't bring myself
to kick them out.

447
00:21:11,966 --> 00:21:14,229
So I built myself a new house.

448
00:21:15,491 --> 00:21:16,710
I'd like to think I've improved

449
00:21:16,840 --> 00:21:18,494
since the first home
that I built.

450
00:21:18,625 --> 00:21:20,104
By the time the puppies

451
00:21:20,235 --> 00:21:21,889
were old enough to start
running around,

452
00:21:22,019 --> 00:21:24,413
the plants were big enough for
me to start harvesting them.

453
00:21:24,544 --> 00:21:26,502
These are tomatoes.

454
00:21:26,633 --> 00:21:29,592
Left alone, they grew
into a tangled mess.

455
00:21:29,723 --> 00:21:33,553
They're pretty hard to harvest,
and they look kind of small.

456
00:21:35,250 --> 00:21:37,818
But they're definitely tomatoes.

457
00:21:37,948 --> 00:21:41,256
The dogs do some hunting and
protect the premises for me.

458
00:21:41,387 --> 00:21:44,651
By the way, it's getting tricky
just calling them all dogs,

459
00:21:44,781 --> 00:21:46,479
so I decided to give them names.

460
00:21:46,609 --> 00:21:49,612
The boy is Kuro,
the girl is Yuki,

461
00:21:49,743 --> 00:21:51,484
even though she's got dark fur.

462
00:21:51,614 --> 00:21:53,355
Kuro, Yuki.

463
00:21:53,486 --> 00:21:55,357
[upbeat music]

464
00:21:55,488 --> 00:21:58,055
I didn't think dogs
would eat vegetables,

465
00:21:58,186 --> 00:22:00,493
but seeing them enjoying
the vegetables so much

466
00:22:00,623 --> 00:22:01,929
makes me want to work harder

467
00:22:02,059 --> 00:22:03,844
to grow better ones
to feed them.

468
00:22:03,974 --> 00:22:07,413
I've been pretty busy with
harvesting vegetables,

469
00:22:07,543 --> 00:22:09,632
which makes me want to
shout with joy.

470
00:22:09,763 --> 00:22:11,591
I'll need to build
a storehouse for them.

471
00:22:11,721 --> 00:22:14,550
I want to build furniture
and tools, too.

472
00:22:14,681 --> 00:22:16,813
There's a lot of stuff
I want to do.

473
00:22:16,944 --> 00:22:19,163
[Hiraku sighs]

474
00:22:19,294 --> 00:22:22,297
- [Hiraku] Well,
there's no rush.

475
00:22:22,428 --> 00:22:24,560
I'll take my time working at it.

476
00:22:24,691 --> 00:22:28,042
["Feel the winds"
by Yui Hizuki plays]

477
00:23:21,922 --> 00:23:23,880
- You want to cross
the mountain?

478
00:23:24,011 --> 00:23:25,795
Listen miss,
unless you're drunk,

479
00:23:25,926 --> 00:23:27,754
you really shouldn't be
saying stuff like that.

480
00:23:27,884 --> 00:23:30,713
Haven't you heard of
The Forest of Death?

481
00:23:30,844 --> 00:23:33,237
That's what's you'll find on
the other side of the mountain.

482
00:23:33,368 --> 00:23:35,631
It's full of dangerous monsters.

483
00:23:35,762 --> 00:23:38,373
If any of them ever came
down here and attacked us,

484
00:23:38,504 --> 00:23:41,158
we'd need guards on duty 24/7.

485
00:23:41,289 --> 00:23:43,726
- Huh.

486
00:23:43,857 --> 00:23:46,294
That might be just what I need.

487
00:23:47,164 --> 00:23:50,994
[upbeat pastoral music]

